# SN-Launcher — example environment
#
# Copy to `.env` if you want one locally. `.env` is gitignored; this file is
# the only one that is committed, and it must never contain a real value.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SN-Launcher needs NO secrets to run. It has no backend, no accounts and no
# telemetry. Everything below is optional and exists only so you can point it at
# your own services later.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Weather. SN-Laucher reads Open-Meteo, which is free, keyless and requires no
# account. Pin a location at build time rather than shipping a runtime location
# prompt (on a wall-mounted tablet nobody ever taps again):
#
#     flutter build apk --release --dart-define=NEST_LAT=-33.8688 --dart-define=NEST_LON=151.2093
#
NEST_LAT=
NEST_LON=

# Device under test (see tool/device.sh).
NEST_DEVICE=192.168.1.100:40967

# ── Google Home / Cast (not yet implemented — reserved) ──────────────────────
# The launcher does not currently talk to Google's cloud. When it does, it will
# need a client id and a refresh token, and those belong in a secrets manager
# or your OS keychain, never in a file that ends up in git history.
GOOGLE_HOME_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_HOME_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Future: MCP bridge (deferred, see README) ───────────────────────────────
# MCPB_AUTH_TOKEN=
# MCPB_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# If a secret is ever committed by accident:
#
#   1. Rotate it first. Assume it is already public — every public forge
#      scrapes new commits continuously, so "I'll delete the file" is not a
#      fix. Deleting it in a later commit leaves it in the history.
#   2. `git filter-repo --path .env --invert-paths` to scrub the history, then
#      force-push and tell anyone who cloned it to re-clone.
#
# Order matters: rotate first, clean second.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────